<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Unwinding Phase: Many believe the function "ends" at the base case; they must understand that the stack must then pop every frame to return the final value.</li>
        <li>Variable Persistence: Believing local variables are shared across calls. Each stack frame has its own unique instance of local data.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

